screen.nyanslate.help.title=Help
screen.nyanslate.help.body=Chat messages and entity name tags are always translated automatically, regardless of the active engine.\n\nPress [G] to open Translation Settings, [P] to translate everything on the current screen, and [R] to translate the item you are pointing at (or the item in your hand when nothing is hovered).\n\nWith "AI" selected, item tooltips and interface text translate automatically just like chat, with no key-press hint shown; pressing [R]/[P] then forces a fresh translation (for example if you want a different result). With "Machine" selected, items and interface text never send a request by themselves: hovering an item, if the tooltip still shows the original text, press [R] once to send only the missing lines, or press it again once every line is already translated to force a full retranslation; interface text works the same way, sent only when you press [P] to scan the whole screen.\n\nAI gives higher quality but uses API usage; Machine is free. Switch the engine on the main settings screen - switching mid-game applies the rules above immediately.\n\n"Fall back to machine translation when AI fails" only applies while AI is selected: when on, a failed AI request still shows a machine translation instead of the original text.\n\nUse the Do-Not-Translate filter to keep server/brand names untouched (case-insensitive, whole words).\n\nRequest Cooldown Settings controls how often new requests are sent and how long misses are batched together before being sent out - raise both if you are being rate-limited.\n\nExport/Import lets you share or reuse a translation file for the current language.
